nutdrv_qx, hunnox subdriver: the battery test.

NUT's hunnox table has no T, so test.battery.start.quick fails ("FAILED")
on the Tescom Leo SmartBox (MEC0003 bridge, hunnox). Probed on the real UPS
on 2026-11-15: string index 0x04 (krauler's
"T") runs a real battery test of about 7 s: Q1 shows utility fail and test
in progress, the inverter carries the load (230 V), the battery goes
13.7 -> 13.4 V, then back to mains. 0x05 (TL, deep test) did nothing, so it
is left out. The megatec table sends the quick test as "T\r".

Applied to NUT 2.8.4 before it is built (scripts/build-nut.sh), so the
bundled nutdrv_qx has it; nutdrv_qx_mec is built from the same source.

--- a/drivers/nutdrv_qx.c
+++ b/drivers/nutdrv_qx.c
@@ -1293,6 +1293,7 @@
 		{ "I\r",	0x0c, },	/* Vendor infos */
 		{ "Q\r",	0x07, },	/* Beeper toggle */
 		{ "C\r",	0x0a, },	/* Cancel shutdown/Load on [0x(0..F)A]*/
+		{ "T\r",	0x04, },	/* Battery test, ~7 s (Tescom Leo SmartBox, 2026-11-15) */
 		{ NULL, 0 }
 	};
 	int	i, ret, index = 0;
